 "description": "The Carro Armato M14/41 was an Italian medium tank from World War II. Essentially a modified version of the M13/40 tank, it was designed to address operational issues encountered in North Africa. The tank was equipped with a more powerful engine, additional fuel and air filters, and improved electrical systems. Approximately 750 of these tanks were produced between 1941 and 1943, with the first models converted from M13/40 tanks. While no longer the most modern or reliable vehicle of its time, the tank was used in the North African campaign and to defend Italy against the Allied invasion. A number of them were also operated by Allied forces and the Wehrmacht. The M14/41 was introduced in Update 1.85 \"Supersonic\" . It stands out in battle for its good mobility, rate of fire, and decent gun. However, it has a large silhouette, mediocre armor, and slow turret rotation speed.",
